{{sbc|Passive:}} Non-{{tip|proc damage|proc}} damage sources deal {{as|{{pp|10 + (45-10)/17*(x-1)|1 to 20 by 1}}|true damage}} {{as|'''bonus''' true damage}} to enemy {{tip|champion|champions}} affected by certain {{tip|crowd control}} effects.
{{sbc|Valid Crowd Control:}}
* {{tip|Immobilize|Immobilizes}}
* {{tip|Blind}}
* {{tip|Disarm}}
* {{tip|Ground}}
* {{tip|Nearsight}}
* {{tip|Polymorph}}
* {{tip|Silence}}
* {{tip|Slow}}
The target must already be impaired prior to the damaging attack or spell in order to trigger the '''bonus''' damage.

{{sbc|Passive:}} Gain an ''Elixir'' upon reaching each of the following levels:
* Level 3: {{ii|Elixir of Avarice}}
* Level 6: {{ii|Elixir of Force}}
* Level 9: {{ii|Elixir of Skill}}
If the inventory is full upon the user becoming eligible to receive {{ii|Elixir of Avarice}} or {{ii|Elixir of Force}}, each item will be granted as soon as an empty slot is available. If the inventory is full upon becoming eligible to receive {{ii|Elixir of Skill}}, the item is consumed automatically.

